Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:56:04

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:44:22

Added. X Play on a game of Your games that is in Steam starts it through Steam (steam://rungameid, Steam started
first when it does not run; owner, 29-10-2026: a game started from the manager); a game not in Steam yet says how it
gets there. Open Steam, a row at the top of Your games, opens Steam's library in Big Picture (A Open Steam). Every
browser of the app opens again in the folder last taken or picked a file in (core's browse.remembered), while it is
there.

Fixed. The Log pane's newest lines were a label that grew past the pane and was cut off at the top (owner,
29-10-2026): they are a view of their own now, its newest line in view, which a finger scrolls; a tap on it shows the
whole log as A does.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 19:16:18

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 18:52:05

Added. The BC250 suite's shadPS4 Manager on the portable window (owner, 29-10-2026: the gaming category, after
RPCS3 Manager; Extract PKG and shadNet come along), laid out as RPCS3 Manager: five cards, shadPS4, Your games,
Settings, shadNet and Log, the actions with a controller button in the row at the bottom. A Install downloads shadPS4
0.20.0 for Windows, the release the BC250 suite's app pins (shadps4-win64-sdl-2026-0.20.0.zip, 32 MB, shadPS4.exe
alone), checks it against the pinned SHA-256 and unpacks it into
%LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-shadps4\emulator\ with shadPS4's portable folder user\ beside
it, where shadPS4 keeps its settings, users, saves, system modules and log (its own rule: a user folder in the folder
it starts in, else %APPDATA%\shadPS4); X Remove shadPS4, with a second press, deletes only its program; Y Update when
another version is there. The shadPS4 pane says when Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime is missing (shadPS4.exe imports
vcruntime140, vcruntime140_1, msvcp140 and msvcp140_atomic_wait). LB Modules: the app's folder browser showing the
.sprx files, X copies the open folder's into shadPS4's module folder, and the pane counts the 24 shadPS4 cannot do
without. RB Packages: Extract PKG, the BC250 app's pkgxtractor unchanged, as a pane: the browser showing the .pkg
files, A on one lists the places (the game folders, the usual places, the package's own folder), A on a place unpacks
it there off the window's thread with the files counted, a game into its ID's folder, an update into ID-UPDATE beside
its game (one there already replaced on a second press, only once every file of the new one was written), a folder
that is there never written into; the place becomes a game folder. Not carried over from the BC250 window: the
preview, salvage mode, the comparisons, renaming to the content ID and the icon viewer. When the app installs shadPS4
and when it opens, it adds shadPS4's quit hotkeys to user\input_config\global.ini (View + Menu, Ctrl+Shift+End). Your
games: the folders with an eboot.bin in the chosen folders, read as the BC250 app reads them, with the time spent in
each; played from Steam, never from the app (owner, 29-10-2026), full screen (shadPS4.exe -f true -g, started in its
folder so it finds user\); A Steam mark and Y Update Steam put them in Steam as "[PS4] <title>" (shadPS4 installed
first), with the game's own pictures and a cover from SteamGridDB with the suite's key (RB Steam artwork); LB Folders,
with the folder browser for the controller. The game folders are the app's, as in the suite's other managers (the
BC250 app keeps them in shadPS4's config.json). Settings in four tabs (Picture, Sound, Controller, In a game: the BC250
app's 12 settings of config.json, shadPS4 0.20.0's keys and defaults; the volume steps through nine values), never
written while shadPS4 runs. shadNet, the BC250 app's shadNet window as a pane of rows (Sign in, Player, shadNet name,
Password, Email, Server, Registration key): A on a text row opens its page with the field alone, A keeps the value in
shadPS4's users.json and config.json at once (made with shadPS4's four default users when shadPS4 never ran, as on
the handheld its window never shows), X Create account, Y Try sign-in, against the server off the window's thread;
the line under the heading says who signs in where and what the last game's sign-in did, from shadPS4's log
(log\shad_log.txt, or <Id>.log). The Log: shadPS4's folder, the system modules and the game folders, and the app's
log; A View log (or a tap) shows the whole log in the app. The suite's buttons (B back, View exit, Menu the
information), the d-pad staying in a pane, no pill in a pane and no user name on the screen or in the log, as in every
app of the suite. A game's pictures on a card that was taken out are none rather than an error (Windows raises for an
empty card slot), so Update Steam still takes its shortcut out. Not carried over from the BC250 app: the controller
state in the header (the handheld's controller is built in), the desktop's volume for shadPS4 (Bazzite's), shadPS4's
own window for its other settings, the command-line extractor, and the drop of a .pkg on the window.

